  "prefLabel": "Fors 303.01 Examinations",
  "priorExpiration": "1998-02-05",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Fors 303.01 Examinations.\n\n(a) The board shall hold examinations through the OPLC.\n\n(b) Whenever the evidence presented in an application does not appear to the OPLC, in consultation with the board, to be conclusive and warranting the issuance of a license, the applicant shall be required to pass a written examination.\n\n(c) The applicant for examination shall pay the fee pursuant to Plc 1002.16 each time they take the examination except for the on re-examination described in (e) below.\n\n(d) The examination shall consist of a written examination, prepared and graded by the New Hampshire board of licensure for foresters or representatives designated by the board.\n\n(e) A candidate failing an examination may apply for re-examination at the expiration of 6 months and shall be entitled to one re-examination without payment of an additional fee. Subsequent re-examinations shall be granted upon payment of the re-examination fee.\n\nSource. #5222, eff 9-11-91; EXPIRED 9-11-97\n\nNew. #6597, INTERIM, eff 10-8-97, EXPIRED: 2-5-98\n\nNew. #6876, eff 10-28-98; ss by #8710, eff 8-25-06; ss by #10544, eff 3-13-14; ss by #13855, eff 3-17-24",
